1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,835
Somewhere right now, someone is typing, any update,

2
00:00:02,835 --> 00:00:04,418
for the fourth time this week.

3
00:00:04,818 --> 00:00:05,993
You paid the deposit.

4
00:00:05,993 --> 00:00:08,289
The designer replied with a read receipt.

5
00:00:08,339 --> 00:00:09,844
Flip it. You deliver the logo,

6
00:00:09,844 --> 00:00:12,520
and the client vanishes faster than free pizza.

7
00:00:12,570 --> 00:00:14,712
The payment worked. The promise didn't.

8
00:00:16,012 --> 00:00:18,956
Meet Kept. Money moves only when a promise is kept.

9
00:00:19,256 --> 00:00:21,531
For freelancers. Plumbers. Suppliers.

10
00:00:21,531 --> 00:00:24,087
Anyone who has ever heard, I'll pay you Friday.

11
00:00:24,537 --> 00:00:26,769
Just say the deal, the way you'd text it.

12
00:00:26,619 --> 00:00:29,074
Pay the designer three hundred. A hundred now,

13
00:00:29,074 --> 00:00:30,714
two hundred when the logo lands.

14
00:00:30,714 --> 00:00:32,880
Refund me if nothing shows in a week.

15
00:00:32,980 --> 00:00:34,715
Claude turns that into promises,

16
00:00:34,715 --> 00:00:36,862
and the exact rules that move the money.

17
00:00:36,912 --> 00:00:38,197
Typing something shady,

18
00:00:38,197 --> 00:00:40,087
like a release fee to unlock your money?

19
00:00:40,087 --> 00:00:42,637
Kept flags the scam before anyone pays.

20
00:00:43,337 --> 00:00:46,610
Then Kept does what no payment app does. It proves the deal.

21
00:00:46,610 --> 00:00:48,175
Every delivery, every deadline,

22
00:00:48,175 --> 00:00:49,855
in every order they could happen.

23
00:00:49,855 --> 00:00:52,615
Sixty-three possible futures for one plumber visit,

24
00:00:52,615 --> 00:00:54,270
checked in two milliseconds.

25
00:00:55,220 --> 00:00:57,445
And it caught a bug a tired lawyer would miss.

26
00:00:57,445 --> 00:00:58,505
Deliver on time,

27
00:00:58,505 --> 00:01:01,117
and the designer still loses two hundred dollars.

28
00:01:02,467 --> 00:01:05,428
So the rules get repaired. Never your promises. Proved,

29
00:01:05,428 --> 00:01:06,852
across every outcome.

30
00:01:07,052 --> 00:01:08,477
And before anyone pays a cent,

31
00:01:08,477 --> 00:01:10,765
you can see every way the deal can end.

32
00:01:11,815 --> 00:01:14,880
You both approve the exact same terms. Same fingerprint.

33
00:01:14,880 --> 00:01:17,403
Read it out loud, like a secret handshake.

34
00:01:17,503 --> 00:01:20,308
Then the money sits with PayPal. Not with a stranger.

35
00:01:20,308 --> 00:01:22,895
Not with us. Honestly, we don't want to hold it.

36
00:01:23,445 --> 00:01:26,610
Under the hood, PayPal authorizes the full amount up front.

37
00:01:26,610 --> 00:01:29,410
Each release captures only its slice and pays it out.

38
00:01:29,410 --> 00:01:31,383
Refunds simply void the rest.

39
00:01:32,033 --> 00:01:34,472
The logo lands. Maya taps accept.

40
00:01:34,722 --> 00:01:37,397
Three hundred dollars, released exactly as proved.

41
00:01:37,397 --> 00:01:38,987
And Sam's phone lights up.

42
00:01:39,437 --> 00:01:42,845
Kept's cut? Seven fifty. Only when money actually moves.

43
00:01:43,495 --> 00:01:45,180
Same engine, different job.

44
00:01:45,180 --> 00:01:47,450
The plumber gets forty dollars for showing up,

45
00:01:47,450 --> 00:01:50,135
and the rest when the sink stops leaking. No show?

46
00:01:50,135 --> 00:01:51,629
Every cent comes home.

47
00:01:52,279 --> 00:01:54,254
Every step is signed and hash-chained.

48
00:01:54,254 --> 00:01:57,484
Anyone can check the receipts in their own browser.

49
00:01:57,484 --> 00:01:58,981
No account, no trust required.

50
00:01:59,231 --> 00:02:01,200
Now, the fun part. Let's cheat.

51
00:02:01,750 --> 00:02:05,132
Change two hundred to two thousand. Bold. Also, broken.

52
00:02:05,582 --> 00:02:07,917
Cover your tracks and re-hash it? Still broken.

53
00:02:07,917 --> 00:02:09,507
Only Kept's key can sign,

54
00:02:09,507 --> 00:02:12,038
and every later entry still points at the truth.

55
00:02:12,138 --> 00:02:13,784
Not even we can rewrite it.

56
00:02:14,934 --> 00:02:16,939
And before you pay anyone, paste their link.

57
00:02:16,939 --> 00:02:19,699
Look-alike sites get caught, right in your browser.

58
00:02:20,449 --> 00:02:23,414
AI agents are about to spend real money for us.

59
00:02:23,414 --> 00:02:26,173
Someone has to make sure they spend it the way we meant.

60
00:02:26,273 --> 00:02:29,205
Now give an AI agent a budget, not your card.

61
00:02:29,405 --> 00:02:33,310
Paper? Paid. Toner? It asks you first. A sixty dollar chair?

62
00:02:33,310 --> 00:02:34,743
Denied. Nice try, robot.

63
00:02:34,793 --> 00:02:37,643
A shop you never approved? Denied. A stolen token?

64
00:02:37,643 --> 00:02:38,574
Not today.

65
00:02:39,024 --> 00:02:42,195
And every decision comes with a reason, in plain English.

66
00:02:42,245 --> 00:02:45,290
Want stricter rules? Replay every real purchase first.

67
00:02:45,290 --> 00:02:48,179
At twenty dollars max, two of these would have been blocked.

68
00:02:48,329 --> 00:02:51,253
Close the budget, and every unused dollar comes home.

69
00:02:52,203 --> 00:02:55,354
Building agents? Kept speaks REST and MCP. One command,

70
00:02:55,354 --> 00:02:58,161
and your agent gets a budget it can't blow.

71
00:02:58,311 --> 00:03:01,526
Or embed Kept in your own platform. One API key,

72
00:03:01,526 --> 00:03:04,196
a few calls, and every cent is accounted for.

73
00:03:04,346 --> 00:03:06,401
Under the hood: Convex for the backend,

74
00:03:06,401 --> 00:03:08,661
PayPal for the money, Claude for the words,

75
00:03:08,661 --> 00:03:11,198
and a verifier that runs right in your browser.

76
00:03:11,948 --> 00:03:14,133
Payments that keep their word. For people,

77
00:03:14,133 --> 00:03:16,069
and for the agents working for them.

78
00:03:16,319 --> 00:03:18,519
Say it. Prove it. Hold it. Keep it.

79
00:03:19,869 --> 00:03:20,651
Kept.
